{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.Sl2PeriodConservedQuantity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.Sl2PeriodConservedQuantity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.sl2Invariant_eq_zeroth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.sl2Invariant_eq_zeroth","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/sl2-period-conserved-quantity.lean#L57-L66","doc":"**Conserved first integral.** The invariant is constant along the whole\norbit of the depth-`2` recurrence: `H_n = H_0` for every `n`. (Induction on `n`,\neach step discharged by `sl2Invariant_succ`.) ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:sl2-period-conserved-quantity","label":"prop:sl2-period-conserved-quantity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/sl2-period-conserved-quantity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.sl2Invariant_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.sl2Invariant_succ","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/sl2-period-conserved-quantity.lean#L45-L55","doc":"**First integral, single step.** If `a` satisfies the depth-`2` recurrence\n`a (n+2) = τ · a (n+1) − a n`, the invariant is unchanged: `H_{n+1} = H_n`.\nPure consequence of substituting the recurrence and expanding (`ring`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.sl2Invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.sl2Invariant","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/sl2-period-conserved-quantity.lean#L40-L43","doc":"The depth-`2` first integral `H_n = a (n+1)² − τ · a (n+1) · a n + a n²`,\nthe discrete energy of the Lucas/Chebyshev recurrence. ","signatureChunk":0}]}